1. OWNERSHIP

This repository and all of its contents — source code, documentation, texts,
designs, images, graphic assets, custom fonts, configuration files and any
other material (the "Work") — are the exclusive property of rezzt.dev and its
author (the "Rightsholder"). The Work is protected by Spanish Royal Legislative
Decree 1/1996 of 12 April, approving the consolidated text of the Intellectual
Property Act, by the Berne Convention for the Protection of Literary and
Artistic Works, and by the other applicable international treaties.

2. RESERVATION OF RIGHTS

All economic rights in the Work — reproduction, distribution, public
communication and transformation — are fully reserved to the Rightsholder. No
license to the Work is granted, whether express or implied, by exhaustion, or
by estoppel or acquiescence.

3. PROHIBITIONS

Except with the prior, express, written authorization of the Rightsholder, no
natural or legal person may:

  a) use, run, deploy or exploit the Work for any purpose, whether commercial
     or non-commercial;
  b) copy, reproduce or store the Work, in whole or in part, with the sole
     exception of the automatic technical copy made by a web browser or by the
     version-control system when consulting the repository;
  c) modify, adapt, translate, refactor or create derivative works from the
     Work;
  d) distribute, publish, publicly communicate, sublicense, sell, rent, lend or
     make the Work, or any part of it, available to the public;
  e) remove, obscure or alter any copyright, authorship or license notices.

4. ACCESS TO THE CODE

Any public availability of the code (for example, in an online repository)
exists solely to allow it to be read and studied for reference purposes. Such
access grants none of the rights listed in clause 3 and does not constitute a
disclosure that exhausts any right of the Rightsholder.

5. MORAL RIGHTS

The author's moral rights in the Work are unwaivable and inalienable under
Article 14 of the Spanish Intellectual Property Act, regardless of anything in
this license.

6. NO WARRANTY AND LIMITATION OF LIABILITY

The Work is made available "as is" and "as available", without warranty of any
kind, express or implied. To the maximum extent permitted by applicable law,
the Rightsholder shall not be liable for any direct, indirect, incidental or
consequential damage arising from access to or use of the Work, whether
authorized or unauthorized. Nothing in this clause excludes or limits liability
that cannot be excluded or limited by law (for example, for willful
misconduct).

7. AUTHORIZATIONS

Any request for authorization to use the Work beyond the limits of this license
must be made in writing to: privacy@rezzt.dev. Silence by the Rightsholder does
not amount to authorization.

8. TERMINATION

Any breach of this license automatically and immediately terminates all
permission to access or consult the Work, without prejudice to any legal action
available to the Rightsholder.

9. GOVERNING LAW AND JURISDICTION

This license is governed by Spanish law. For the resolution of any dispute
arising from the Work or this license, the parties submit to the courts of the
Rightsholder's domicile, unless a mandatory rule establishes a different forum
(for example, in relations with consumers).

10. SEVERABILITY

If any provision of this license is held to be void or unenforceable, the
remaining provisions shall remain in full force and effect.
